Z||000006||CoolBlue87GT||12-14-2001||07:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by malacite:<BR><B>my brother i law worked at a radioshack in CT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I work at a RadioShack in Florida, Many people bring in their Portable phones complaining it never charged the batteries.<P>When we open the battery cover, the battery is never plugged in.<P>They get that "deer caught in the headlights look", and say "oh"<P>Then we tell them, the phone was wrapped in a paper that said, Stop, plug in the battery.<P>They always say, oh I tore that off & threw it away without looking at it.<P>More guy's do this, the gal's read more directions than guys.||||reg||6
Z||000007||Formula88||12-15-2001||12:16 AM||||I've got a list of I.T. Help Desk horror stories somewhere, but I'll relay my favorite as best as memory allows.<P>Help Desk:  Can I help you?<BR>User:  I can't get Word Perfect to work<BR>HD:  Ok, are you in Word Perfect now?<BR>U:  No<BR>HD:  Well, open Word Perfect.<BR>U:  I can't.<BR>HD:  Why not?<BR>U:  I can't see the icons.<BR>HD:  Why not?<BR>U:  The monitor's blank.<BR>HD:  Is the monitor on?<BR>U:  I don't know.<BR>HD:  Is there a light lit on the front of the monitor?<BR>U:  I can't see one.  I don't think so.<BR>HD:  Ok.  Is the monitor plugged in?<BR>U:  I don't know.<BR>HD:  Well, I want you to check and see if it's plugged in.<BR>U:  I can't see if it's plugged in.<BR>HD:  Well, grab the two cables in the back of the monitor and see if one goes to the PC and the other goes to the power outlet.<BR>U:  I can't see that either.<BR>HD:  Can't you get behind the PC?<BR>U:  No, it's not that.  It's too dark in here. The lights are off.<BR>HD:  Well, turn on the lights.<BR>U:  I can't.  There's been a power failure.<P>HD:  [sound of screaming over the phone.... and the line goes dead]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierospeeder||12-15-2001||03:31 AM||||anyone still have that link of the help line for computers,  greatest idiot moments?<P>i know this was posted before.||||reg||1
Z||000009||TRiAD||12-15-2001||02:13 PM||||At the Peoria Courthouse, I had a client who called in and had a problem with Word in WIN95, she was completely locked up. With the old systems we used there, rebooting was generally the only way to fix anything. Made my job pretty easy, most days. <P>Anyway, so I ask what she was trying to do, ask if she'd been saving as she went along (WHY do people NOT do this?!), and inevitably had her reboot. Here you go...<P>HD (me); "OK, well, we both knew it would come to this, go ahead and..."<BR>Client; "Reboot? OK...(insert 2 seconds here)it didn't work."<BR>HD; "Um, what do you mean?"<BR>C; "Well, it didn't help..."<BR>HD; "Can you tell me what's currently on your screen?"<BR>C; "Yeah, the error is still there, right where I left it."<BR>HD; "Huh, not sure how that can be, you were in the middle of Word, and it shouldn't have re-launched when you rebooted...Can you reboot again for me?"<BR>C; "Sure...nope, didn't work."<BR>HD; "Huh?! That was fast...tell you what, walk me through your reboot procedure."<BR>C; "Man, you guys NEVER fix anything right! Here...I push the button..."<BR>HD; "Which button?"<BR>C; "The reboot button...and I hit it again to turn it back on..."<BR>HD; "Where is this button located on your machine?"<BR>C; "It's right there, on the computer!"<BR>HD; "Is it on the CPU, or on the monitor?"<BR>C; "Well, I don't know! It's right there in front of me!..."<BR>HD; "Let me rephrase...is it on the part that you put disks into, or the part you look at?"<BR>C; "It's on the part I look at, right there in front of me, can you just send someone up again?!"<P>She was hitting the power button on the monitor to reboot...<P>I had her reboot properly, and she was fine, except losing 2 hours of work, since she never saved as she went...<P>She was forevermore infamous in the IT department...<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000010||Formula88||12-15-2001||11:40 PM||||Actually, turning off the monitor to "reboot" is fairly common at my employer.  If I tell them to turn off the box on the desk, they reply, "Oh, you want me to turn off my Hard Drive?  I thought you just wanted the computer turned off."||||reg||1
