Z||000016||Jaygee79||12-17-2001||01:01 AM||||here's one from the reader's digest:<P>It seemed that all our appliances had broken in the same week, and repairs were straining our budget.  So when I picked up the kids from school and our jeep started making rattling sounds, I decided that rather than burden my husband, I'd deal with it.  I hadn't reckoned on my little tattle-tales, however.  They rushed into the house with the news: "Daddy, the Jeep was breaking down, but mom made the noise stop!"  Impressed, my husband asked, "How did you fix it?"  "I turned up the radio," I confessed.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Blacktree||12-17-2001||03:25 AM||||IDIOTS AT WORK PARTE DEUX:<P>While on lunch break, I met a couple coworkers talking about car stuff. One of the guys was planning to buy a new car and was trying to decide what car to buy. Being a gearhead, I joined the conversation. After talking about different engines, body styles, etc I asked him "so would you prefer a stick shift or a manual transmission?" After a few seconds of thought, he replied with "I think I'd go with a stick shift".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>MILITARY INTELLIGENCE:<P>While in the service, I got to drive Hummers quite a lot. Once when we were out in the field, one of our Hummers started running a little rough. Our platoon had a rookie lieutenant fresh out of OCS, and he knew I was a gearhead, so he asked me to help him find the problem with the Hummer. We popped open the hood and checked out the engine. After a few minutes of poking and prodding, he asked me what I thought was wrong. So I said "well, the spark plugs probably need to be replaced". The lieutenant then drove the Hummer to the motor pool to have them replace the spark plugs. (Hummers have diesel engines, which don't use spark plugs) <P>The next morning I was put on KP detail  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A><p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-17-2001).]||||reg||1
